            "review_title": "Review at Texas Chicken",
            "review_text": "Ajarn Mark\nBangkok, Thailand73 contributions\n0\nBad service and maintenance\nAug 2015 • Family\nI went to this restaurant and tried to wash hands but the soap dispenser was broken and you really have to wrestle with that to get few small drops of liquid soap. I asked to talk to the manager, so one girl said that she is manager and when I told her the issue then she ask another girl and told me that she is the manager (so apparently, she would just pretend to be manager). The \"actual\" manager confirmed that the first girl is only shift supervisor. So I told her the problem and she told me that why dont I just wrestle with the dispenser to get the soap as \"no one has ever claimed that it is broken\". She asked me if I want to talk to area operations manager, which I really wanted to, so she went to him (he was sitting on one table with his friend/staff), however, he refused to talk to me. Later the manager called the repair service guys and the installed the new dispenser. However, when I went to get the drinks, there was no ice in the beverage dispenser and one girl immediately took our glasses and brought ice from some other place within the restaurant. So, I simply asked the manager, why so much disorganization, to which she replied that she just joined two days ago. Apparently, the place was poorly managed and I don't want to imagine how dirty their kitchen would be, if they don't have soap for the customers.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten September 1, 2015",
